<!-- kait2en-copr -->
COPR test kernel built successfully.

- Experiment: `@EXPERIMENT@`
- Fedora kernel base: `@BASE_KVER@`
- Build: @BUILD_URL@
- COPR: `@COPR_PROJECT@`
- Kernel NVR: `@NVR@`
- Kernel release: `@KVER@`

Install:

```bash
sudo dnf copr enable @COPR_PROJECT@
sudo dnf install kernel-@NVR@ kernel-devel-@NVR@
sudo reboot
```

Remove:

```bash
sudo dnf remove kernel-@NVR@ kernel-devel-@NVR@
sudo dnf copr disable @COPR_PROJECT@
```

Warnings:

- If it does not boot, select the Fedora kernel in GRUB's advanced menu or use
  `kait2en-rescue` from the live USB.
- On T2 Macs with an AMD dGPU, `install-gpu-runtime-pm.sh` cannot obtain this
  COPR kernel's SRPM from Koji. Its AMDGPU runtime-PM patches are therefore
  absent.
